    "# Induction Heads — first poke at Pythia-70M\n",
    "\n",
    "Starting point: Olsson et al. (2022) claim induction heads are \"universal\" across transformer architectures.\n",
    "That's a strong claim. Before I believe it, I want to see it myself on a small model.\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook is pure scratchpad. I'll clean things up later if results look interesting.\n",
    "\n",
    "Plan:\n",
    "1. Load Pythia-70M via TransformerLens\n",
    "2. Construct the canonical repeated-token sequence `[A][B]...[A] → [B]`\n",
    "3. Compute induction scores per head\n",
    "4. Eyeball attention patterns to make sure the scores make sense\n",
    "5. Try a few different sequences to sanity check\n",
    "\n",
    "Questions I have going in:\n",
    "- Do induction heads cluster in specific layers, or are they spread out?\n",
    "- Is the score threshold arbitrary, or does it fall out of the distribution naturally?\n",
    "- What does an 'almost-induction-head' look like?\n",
    "\n",
    "Reference: https://transformer-circuits.pub/2022/in-context-learning-and-induction-heads/index.html"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
