    "print(f'Context length: {model.cfg.n_ctx}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. The repeated-token test sequence\n",
    "\n",
    "Classic induction head test: construct a sequence like\n",
    "\n",
    "`[BOS] t_0 t_1 t_2 ... t_{n-1} [SEP?] t_0 t_1 t_2 ...`\n",
    "\n",
    "An induction head at position `n + k` should attend strongly back to position `k`\n",
    "(the first occurrence of the current token). The induction *score* is defined as:\n",
    "the average attention an induction head places on the token immediately following\n",
    "its previous occurrence.\n",
    "\n",
    "Olsson et al. use random tokens for the first half. Let me try that first, then\n",
    "also try with a real sentence repeated to see if it matters."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Helper from induction_score.py\n",
    "# repeated_token_sequence(model, seq_len=50, seed=42)\n",
    "# returns shape [1, 2*seq_len + 1] (includes BOS)\n",
    "\n",
    "seq_len = 50  # length of each half\n",
    "tokens = repeated_token_sequence(model, seq_len=seq_len, seed=42)\n",
    "print(f'Token sequence shape: {tokens.shape}')\n",
    "print(f'Token sequence: {tokens[0, :10].tolist()} ... (first 10 of {tokens.shape[1]})')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Sanity check: second half should be identical to first half\n",
    "first_half = tokens[0, 1:seq_len+1]  # skip BOS\n",
    "second_half = tokens[0, seq_len+1:]\n",
    "assert torch.all(first_half == second_half), 'repeat structure broken'\n",
    "print('Repeat structure verified ✓')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
