   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Compute induction scores\n",
    "\n",
    "Definition from Olsson et al.:\n",
    "> The induction score for head h in layer l is the average attention\n",
    "> that head places on the token at position (pos - seq_len + 1) in the second\n",
    "> half of the repeated sequence.\n",
    "\n",
    "Basically: for each position `i` in the second half, how much does head `(l, h)`\n",
    "attend to position `i - seq_len + 1`? Average that over the second half.\n",
    "\n",
    "Score of 1.0 = perfect induction head. Score near 0 = not doing induction."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# compute_induction_scores is in src/induction_score.py\n",
    "# returns dict with 'scores' array of shape [n_layers, n_heads]\n",
    "# and some metadata\n",
    "\n",
    "results = compute_induction_scores(model, tokens, cache)\n",
    "scores = results['scores']  # [n_layers, n_heads]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Score array shape: {scores.shape}')\n",
    "print(f'Score range: [{scores.min():.4f}, {scores.max():.4f}]')\n",
    "print(f'Mean score: {scores.mean():.4f}')\n",
    "print()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Print per-layer stats\n",
    "print('Per-layer max induction score:')\n",
    "for layer_idx in range(model.cfg.n_layers):\n",
    "    layer_max = scores[layer_idx].max()\n",
    "    best_head = scores[layer_idx].argmax()\n",
    "    print(f'  Layer {layer_idx}: max={layer_max:.4f} (head {best_head})')"
   ]
  },
